{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZuFgK5Mb9zH4hxswaft","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — Verified with `mvnw clean compile`, BUILD SUCCESS\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All original tests (OrderControllerTest, ShipmentControllerTest, CustomerControllerTest, SampleServiceApplicationTests) still pass: 20 tests total, 0 failures\n3. ✅ **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's CREATED shipments** — Covered by:\n   - Test: `cancels an active order and returns 200` ✓\n   - Test: `cancels an active order and its created shipments` ✓\n   - Implementation: OrderController.cancel() sets order.status = CANCELLED and saves it; iterates through shipments and cancels CREATED ones\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — Uses same patterns:\n   - ResourceNotFoundException for 404 (order not found)\n   - ConflictException for 409 (confirmed shipment blocks cancel; cancelled order blocks shipment creation)\n   - ApiError envelope with error.code and error.message\n5. ✅ **A repeated cancel succeeds; a cancel blocked by a CONFIRMED shipment changes nothing; an unknown order is refused; a shipment for a cancelled order is refused** — Covered by:\n   - Test: `cancelling an already cancelled order succeeds without changes` ✓\n   - Test: `cancel is rejected if a shipment is confirmed` (verifies order stays ACTIVE and shipment stays CONFIRMED) ✓\n   - Test: `cancel returns 404 for a non-existent order` ✓\n   - Test: `rejects shipment creation for a cancelled order` ✓\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** — Only modified .kt files and test files, no pom.xml changes\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only changed:\n   - Order.kt (added status field and OrderStatus enum)\n   - OrderRepository.kt (added findByOrderId method to ShipmentRepository, not OrderRepository)\n   - OrderController.kt (added cancel endpoint)\n   - ShipmentRepository.kt (added findByOrderId method)\n   - ShipmentController.kt (added cancelled order validation)\n   - ApiError.kt (added error codes)\n   - Plus corresponding test files\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — ✅ Required: Added `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field to Order data class and added OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED. This is necessary for the feature.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** — Actually, I didn't need to modify this file. Let me check my changes to ShipmentRepository.kt again. Yes, I added findByOrderId to ShipmentRepository, not OrderRepository. This is necessary to find shipments by order when cancelling.\n\n3. **OrderController.kt** — ✅ Required: Added cancel endpoint, injected ShipmentRepository for querying shipments. This is where the feature lives.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — ✅ Required: Added findByOrderId method needed to query shipments when cancelling an order.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — ✅ Required: Added check to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders. Injected OrderRepository to check order status.\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** — ✅ Required: Added ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and ORDER_IS_CANCELLED error codes for the new failure cases.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — ✅ Required: Added comprehensive tests for cancel scenarios. Updated reset() to clear both repositories.\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — ✅ Required: Added test for shipment creation rejection on cancelled order. Updated reset() to clear both repositories.\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. All requirements have been addressed with tests and implementation.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement   Customers can cancel active orders until a shipment is confirmed, with order status tracking and cascading shipment cancellations\nChanged       Order.kt: Added status field with OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED)\n              OrderController.kt: Added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with atomicity and idempotency\n              ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId method for discovering shipments to cancel\n              ShipmentController.kt: Added validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n              ApiError.kt: Added error codes ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and ORDER_IS_CANCELLED\n              OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 6 new tests for cancel scenarios and status verification\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added test for rejected shipment creation on cancelled order\nTests         1. cancelActiveOrderWithoutShipments: Order transitions to CANCELLED\n              2. cancelActiveOrderWithCreatedShipments: Order and CREATED shipments transition to CANCELLED\n              3. cancellingAlreadyCancelledOrderSucceedsWithoutChanges: Idempotent cancel behavior\n              4. cancelRejectedByConfirmedShipment: 409 conflict, no state changes when CONFIRMED shipment exists\n              5. cancelReturns404ForNonExistentOrder: Proper not found handling\n              6. newlyCreatedOrdersHaveActiveStatus: Default status verification\n              7. rejectShipmentCreationForCancelledOrder: 409 conflict when creating shipment for cancelled order\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS, 20 tests passed (4 original OrderControllerTest + 6 new cancel tests + 5 original ShipmentControllerTest + 1 new shipment test + 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests + 3 CustomerControllerTest)\nNot done      Nothing - all acceptance criteria implemented and verified"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":40365,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":793},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformation